@startuml MCP Integration Workflow

!theme plain
title SABER MCP Integration - Header-Based Session Mapping (MCP Compliant)

actor Agent
participant "SABERMCPClient" as MCPClient
participant "MCPClient\n(Raw)" as RawMCP
participant "SABERRestClient" as RESTClient
participant "SessionRestAPI\n(REST)" as REST
participant "SessionMCPAPI\n(MCP Component)" as MCP
participant "SessionManager" as SM
participant "ExecutionManager" as EM_EXEC
participant "EpisodeManager" as EM_EP
participant "MCPToolGenerator" as ToolGen

== Session Initialization (REST First) ==
Agent -> RESTClient: create_session(client_id)
RESTClient -> REST: POST /session
REST -> SM: create_session(client_id)
SM -> REST: ClientSession
REST -> RESTClient: session_id
RESTClient -> Agent: session_id

== MCP Connection with Session Headers ==
Agent -> MCPClient: connect()
note right: MCPClient initialized with:\n- session_id from REST\n- task_id (optional)\n- client_id
MCPClient -> RawMCP: connect(sse_url, headers)
note right: Headers: X-SABER-Session-ID, X-SABER-Task-ID, X-SABER-Client-ID
RawMCP -> MCP: SSE connection with headers
MCP -> MCP: _get_session_from_headers()
note right: Extracts session_id from headers\nNo session creation - maps to existing session
MCP -> RawMCP: connection established
RawMCP -> MCPClient: connected

== Tool Discovery (Dynamic Registration) ==
Agent -> MCPClient: list_tools()
MCPClient -> RawMCP: list_tools()
RawMCP -> MCP: handle_list_tools()
MCP -> SM: get_execution_manager()
SM -> EM_EXEC: to_mcp_tools()
EM_EXEC -> ToolGen: get_available_executors()
ToolGen -> EM_EXEC: dynamic_tool_schemas[]
note right of EM_EXEC: Returns clean tool schemas:\n- python(code)\n- cli(command)\n- end_episode(submission)
EM_EXEC -> MCP: executor_tools + hardcoded_tools
MCP -> RawMCP: mcp_tools[]
RawMCP -> MCPClient: available_tools[]
MCPClient -> Agent: tools_list[]

== Command Execution (Header-Based Session Context) ==
Agent -> MCPClient: python(code="print('hello')")
MCPClient -> MCPClient: check_episode_terminated()
note right: HARD TERMINATION:\nBlocks all calls if episode ended
MCPClient -> RawMCP: call_tool("python", {code: "print('hello')"})
RawMCP -> MCP: handle_call_tool("python", args)
MCP -> MCP: _get_session_from_headers()
note right: Session context retrieved\nfrom HTTP headers,\nnot tool parameters
MCP -> MCP: _convert_to_action(tool_name, args)
MCP -> SM: execute_action(session_id, action)
SM -> EM_EXEC: step(action, context)
EM_EXEC -> SM: CommandResult
SM -> EM_EP: step(session_id, action, result)
EM_EP -> SM: step_result
SM -> MCP: CommandResult
MCP -> MCP: _convert_to_mcp_result(CommandResult)
MCP -> RawMCP: mcp_result
RawMCP -> MCPClient: tool_response
MCPClient -> MCPClient: _monitor_response(response)
note right: Monitors for episode termination\nsignals and updates internal state
MCPClient -> Agent: command_result

== Episode End (Clean Tool + Monitoring) ==
Agent -> MCPClient: end_episode(submission="flag{found}")
MCPClient -> RawMCP: call_tool("end_episode", {submission: "flag{found}"})
RawMCP -> MCP: _handle_end_episode_call(args)
MCP -> MCP: _get_session_from_headers()
MCP -> SM: execute_action(session_id, result_action)
note right: Records submission first
MCP -> SM: end_episode(session_id, "agent_completed", result)
SM -> EM_EP: end_current_episode()
EM_EP -> SM: episode_ended
SM -> MCP: CommandResult(success)
MCP -> RawMCP: success_result
RawMCP -> MCPClient: episode_ended_response
MCPClient -> MCPClient: _episode_terminated = True
MCPClient -> Agent: episode_completed

== Session Cleanup ==
Agent -> MCPClient: disconnect()
MCPClient -> RawMCP: disconnect()
RawMCP -> MCP: connection_closed
Agent -> RESTClient: terminate_session() (optional)
RESTClient -> REST: DELETE /session/{id}
REST -> SM: terminate_session(session_id)
SM -> SM: cleanup_session_resources()

note right of MCP
**MCP Compliance Achieved**
✅ Clean tool schemas (no session_id)
✅ Header-based session mapping
✅ Pure functional parameters
✅ Standard MCP client compatibility
✅ SSE transport with headers

**Actual Tool Examples:**
- python(code: str)
- cli(command: str)
- end_episode(submission?: str)

**Key Implementation Details:**
- Uses fastmcp.server.dependencies.get_http_headers()
- Dynamic tool registration via MCPToolGenerator
- Episode termination monitoring in SABERMCPClient
end note

note right of REST
**SessionRestAPI Responsibilities**
- Session lifecycle management (create/terminate)
- Episode management (start/end)
- Task configuration and policies
- Benchmark information access
- Health checks and status
- Event streaming (SSE)
end note

note right of SM
**Dual Protocol Architecture**
- REST API for session/episode management
- MCP API for clean tool execution
- Header-based session context mapping
- Separate client types: SABERRestClient + SABERMCPClient
- No automatic session creation via MCP
- Resource cleanup on session termination
end note

note right of MCPClient
**SABERMCPClient Features**
- Wraps raw MCPClient for enhanced functionality
- Episode termination monitoring (_episode_terminated)
- Hard termination: blocks calls after episode ends
- Optional monitoring callbacks for harness integration
- Session context passed via HTTP headers only
end note

@enduml
